# Context-root ignore list for the Viewer image build.
#
# BuildKit does NOT read this file for viewer/Dockerfile: it prefers
# viewer/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which REPLACES this one (see the notes in
# there, they are the authoritative list). The classic builder, which is
# what `docker build` still is on a stock Debian docker.io install without
# the buildx plugin, ignores that per-Dockerfile file and reads THIS one.
# The Dockerfile ends its build stage with `COPY . .`, so on that builder
# the build context is the image, and a build from a working tree (rather
# than the clean checkout CI uses) would otherwise drag in installed
# modules, build output, secrets and the nested private repositories.
#
# Every pattern that must catch a nested path is `**/`-prefixed: Docker
# matches against the path relative to the context root, so a bare `.env*`
# would exclude only /.env* and leave viewer/.env.local in. `dist` is
# deliberately NOT here: dist/bridge-bundle.js must reach the image.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.verify-artifacts
tasks
docs
website
.claude
CLAUDE.md
desktop/release
desktop/dist
desktop/.signed-keep
ai-gateway-prototype
.desde-viewer
.prototools-viewer
*.log
